TYPES.md §9.3, EVALUATION.md §7.1, §8.3, log-2026-11-01 "NOTENTRY report": a block check reading
self.id, and a one-line check reading self.retired then self.id, on lr, no entry: E4003 at the first
selection each run evaluates. A check reading neither runs on lr as before: E5001.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// A row.
record Row {
  /// Its code.
  code: String

  check {
    if self.id == "" {
      fail(code, "no id")
    }
  }

  check both: self.retired or self.id != "" else "neither"

  check short: code != "y" else "code y"
}

/// The rows.
let ta: table Row = { a { code: "a" } }

/// A row that is no entry.
let lr: Row = { code: "y" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E4003]  a/a.canon:10:8
  lr: .id of a value that is not an entry of a table or keyed list

error[E4003]  a/a.canon:15:15
  lr: .retired of a value that is not an entry of a table or keyed list

error[E5001]  a/a.canon:24:15
  lr: code y
  expected by a/a.canon:17 (check short)

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
